From 5a198bd59ea8d92f35d2f6699e9f00052fd74ed5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mateusz Bajorski <mbajorski@shasta.cloud>
Date: Tue, 10 Mar 2026 09:12:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] zedagent: fix UUID mismatch rejecting LOC configs

inhaleDeviceConfig checks config.GetId().Uuid against the device UUID
and returns invalidConfig if they differ, silently dropping the entire
LOC config without publishing any AppInstanceConfig.

LOC configs don't carry a device UUID assertion (they're served locally
and don't need to identify the device), so remove the Id field from
gen-loc-config output. The nil Id is already safe: inhaleDeviceConfig
skips the UUID check when Id is nil.

Also fix the remaining config.GetId().Uuid field access (non-nil-safe)
in parseAppInstanceConfig to use the proto getter GetUuid() instead,
consistent with the earlier fix in parseedgenodeinfo.go.

Signed-off-by: Mateusz Bajorski <mbajorski@shasta.cloud>
---
 pkg/pillar/cmd/zedagent/parseconfig.go | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/pkg/pillar/cmd/zedagent/parseconfig.go b/pkg/pillar/cmd/zedagent/parseconfig.go
index 9a12ceeb1..ad11be724 100644
--- a/pkg/pillar/cmd/zedagent/parseconfig.go
+++ b/pkg/pillar/cmd/zedagent/parseconfig.go
@@ -644,7 +644,7 @@ func parseAppInstanceConfig(getconfigCtx *getconfigContext,
 		appinstancePrevConfigHash, configHash, Apps)
 	appinstancePrevConfigHash = configHash
 
-	devUUIDStr := config.GetId().Uuid
+	devUUIDStr := config.GetId().GetUuid()
 
 	// First look for deleted ones. Look for Apps that exists on EVE OS, but not in the config
 	// file from the server. If yes, we will remove the App from the EVE OS.
